---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteMasthead from '../components/SiteMasthead.astro';
const description = 'Irregular Pearl is a nonprofit organization dedicated to making classical music knowledge more accessible, supporting emerging artists, and cultivating a connected community around classical music.';
const jsonLd = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'About Irregular Pearl', description, url: Astro.url.href };
---
<Layout title="About Irregular Pearl" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <SiteMasthead showAbout={false} />
  <main class="who-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Our Mission</span></nav>
    <article>
      <h1>About Irregular Pearl</h1>
      <div class="who-copy" id="our-mission">
        <p>Irregular Pearl is a nonprofit organization dedicated to making classical music knowledge more accessible, supporting emerging artists, and cultivating a connected community around classical music. Through education, artistic opportunities, and community participation, we hope to encourage a culture of curiosity, generosity, and shared discovery.</p>
        <h2>Making Classical Music Knowledge Accessible</h2>
        <p>In all fields, knowledge is power. Yet within classical music, valuable information and practical insights can be surprisingly difficult to find. Resources are often scattered across publications, archives, specialized websites, and informal professional networks, making it challenging for those without established connections or prior experience to navigate the field.</p>
        <p>Irregular Pearl provides a platform to bring this knowledge into a centralized, open-access space where performers, composers, musicologists, researchers, educators, students, and enthusiasts can both learn from and contribute to a shared body of knowledge. By combining community participation with editorial oversight, we aim to develop a reliable, continually evolving resource that reflects the breadth of experience and expertise within the classical music world.</p>
        <h2>Supporting Emerging Classical Artists</h2>
        <p>The future of classical music depends, in part, on the opportunities available to its next generation of performers and composers. Yet developing a professional career in music can require significant resources, connections, and opportunities that are not equally accessible to everyone.</p>
        <p>Through charitable support and dedicated initiatives, Irregular Pearl is working to help emerging artists develop their careers by creating performance opportunities, connecting them with professional resources, and supporting their artistic growth.</p>
        <p>Our Resident Artist Program is an early step toward this mission, providing selected emerging musicians with opportunities to perform as concerto soloists with established orchestras. As the organization grows, we hope to expand our support for individual musicians and composers while helping bring live classical music to broader audiences.</p>
        <h2>Cultivating a Community Around Classical Music</h2>
        <p>Classical music is more than an academic discipline or a professional pursuit. It is also a source of enjoyment, curiosity, conversation, and shared cultural experience.</p>
        <p>Irregular Pearl aspires to provide a welcoming digital space where people from all backgrounds develop their interests together. Whether someone is a professional musician, a student, or simply curious about classical music, we hope they can find a place in this community.</p>
        <h2>Our Vision</h2>
        <p>Ultimately, Irregular Pearl seeks to bring knowledge, opportunity, and community together in one evolving space. We envision a classical music culture in which expertise is generously shared, emerging artists are meaningfully supported, and people from all walks of life feel encouraged to discover and participate. Our hope is that Irregular Pearl will grow not only as a resource for classical music, but as a community shaped by the people who contribute to it.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>

  .who-shell { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px 72px; }
  .breadcrumbs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .breadcrumbs a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .breadcrumbs a:focus-visible { outline: 1px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  article { max-width: 680px; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 24px; font: 500 26px/1.25 var(--font-serif); }
  .who-copy { padding-top: 24px; border-top: .5px solid var(--border); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink); }
  .who-copy p { margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .who-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .who-copy h2 { margin: 32px 0 16px; font: 500 22px/1.3 var(--font-serif); }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .who-shell { padding: 40px 32px 88px; } }
  @media (max-width: 767px) { .who-copy { font-size: 15px; } }
</style>
